 ('6.110','replace',('through 6.115','through 6.116')),
 ('6.111','replace',('(See §§ 6.715, 6.740, and 6.742.)','(See §§ 6.116, 6.740, 6.742 and 6.743.)')),
 ('6.116','add',('Limiting height and speeds for safe landing following power failure.','Subpart B - Flight','If a range of heights exists at any speed, including zero, within which it is not possible to make a safe landing following power failure, the range of heights and its variation with forward speed shall be established together with any other pertinent information, such as type of landing surface. Such an envelope shall be established in full autorotation for single-engine helicopters and with one engine inoperative for multiengine helicopters provided that engine isolation design features are incorporated to assure continued operation of the remaining engines. (See § 6.743 (c).)')),
 ('6.121','append',('(e) Controllability after power failure shall be demonstrated over the range of air speeds and altitudes for which certification is sought, starting with maximum continuous power at critical weight. In taking corrective action, the time delay for all flight conditions shall be based on the normal pilot reaction time, except that for the cruise condition the time delay shall not be less than one second.',)),
 ('6.123','replace',('necessary to obtain and maintain speeds below','necessary to obtain speeds below')),
